---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Overview">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#fafafa] mb-6">Product Overview</h1>
  <p class="text-[#a1a1aa] leading-relaxed mb-8">
    Wago is a lightweight, self-hosted service that connects a WhatsApp account via QR authentication and exposes REST API endpoints for automated message dispatch. Built with Express, TypeScript, and Baileys.
  </p>

  <hr class="border-[#1a1a1a] my-8" />

  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[#fafafa] mb-4">Core Capabilities</h2>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-8">
    <div class="border border-[#1a1a1a] rounded-lg p-4">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#fafafa] mb-1">QR Authentication</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-[#71717a]">Authenticate via Baileys WhatsApp Web QR stream directly in browser or raw terminal string.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="border border-[#1a1a1a] rounded-lg p-4">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#fafafa] mb-1">Session Persistence</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-[#71717a]">Stores auth keys in multi-file storage (<code class="text-[#a1a1aa] bg-[#1a1a1a] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">/app/data/auth</code>), surviving process and container restarts.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="border border-[#1a1a1a] rounded-lg p-4">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#fafafa] mb-1">Text Message Dispatch</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-[#71717a]">Send text messages instantly to any valid WhatsApp recipient with automatic phone normalization.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="border border-[#1a1a1a] rounded-lg p-4">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#fafafa] mb-1">API Key Security</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-[#71717a]">Web bootstrap authorization, HttpOnly session cookies, and Bearer token key enforcement.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <hr class="border-[#1a1a1a] my-8" />

  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[#fafafa] mb-4">Phone Number Normalization</h2>
  <p class="text-[#a1a1aa] text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">
    The backend normalizes phone numbers before generating WhatsApp JIDs:
  </p>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-sm text-[#a1a1aa] space-y-1.5 mb-8">
    <li>Strips whitespace, hyphens, and leading <code class="text-[#a1a1aa] bg-[#1a1a1a] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">+</code> signs.</li>
    <li>Converts local Indonesian numbers starting with <code class="text-[#a1a1aa] bg-[#1a1a1a] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">08...</code> into <code class="text-[#a1a1aa] bg-[#1a1a1a] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">628...</code>.</li>
    <li>Result: <code class="text-[#a1a1aa] bg-[#1a1a1a] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">0813-6563-0011</code> becomes <code class="text-[#a1a1aa] bg-[#1a1a1a] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">6281365630011@s.whatsapp.net</code></li>
  </ul>

  <hr class="border-[#1a1a1a] my-8" />

  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[#fafafa] mb-4">Security</h2>
  <p class="text-[#a1a1aa] text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">The application enforces strict security controls:</p>
  <div class="border border-[#1a1a1a] rounded-lg divide-y divide-[#1a1a1a] text-sm mb-8">
    <div class="p-4">
      <p class="font-medium text-[#fafafa] mb-1">Web Bootstrap</p>
      <p class="text-[#71717a]">Enabled with <code class="text-[#a1a1aa] bg-[#141414] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">ALLOW_WEB_BOOTSTRAP=true</code>. Generates a secure API key on initial run and sets an HttpOnly cookie.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="p-4">
      <p class="font-medium text-[#fafafa] mb-1">Bearer Auth</p>
      <p class="text-[#71717a]">Protected endpoints require <code class="text-[#a1a1aa] bg-[#141414] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">Authorization: Bearer &lt;API_KEY&gt;</code>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
